  a)non repeatable read problem
  b)dirty read problem
  c)panthom read problem

=>oracle supports two types of locking
    1)Exclusive lock
    2)shared lock
=>two users cannot update the same data at the same time.


=>concurrent access means accessing same data by number of people at the same time

ex:railway ticket booking

oracle supports two types of locking:
====================================

Exclusive Lock Mode:
====================

=>it will prevent associate resource from updating the content,only the locked resource can
          alter the content.

Shared Lock Mode:
================

=>allows the associated resource to be shared,several transactions can acquire share locks
   on same reosurce

Row Level lock:
==============

=>locking entire row

Table level lock:
===============

=>entire table will be locked

=>SQL>LOCK TABLE <TABLENAME> IN EXCLUSIVE MODE;

=>SQL>LOCK TABLE EMP IN SHARE MODE

EX:LOCK TABLE SCOTT.EMP IN EXCLUSIVE MODE;
